NTV Forge 1.2.4a — Late Subtitle Synchronization (experimental)

Changes relative to 1.2.4:
- Corrected diagnostic version identifier.
- WebVTT subtitle segments now carry an X-TIMESTAMP-MAP mapping their
  cue times to the actual MPEG-TS presentation timestamp for that segment.
- FFprobe reads each requested segment's transport clock, cached per session.
- A lightweight background sampler captures each clip's initial transport
  timestamp even if captions are switched off until several minutes later.
- Actual transport timing is preferred over reconstructed segment durations.
- Diagnostics now report the timing source, MPEG-TS timestamp and map status.
- No changes to the FFmpeg encoder configuration, HLS video muxer, UI or
  channel export behavior.

Test: Start a captioned YouTube channel with subtitles OFF. Enable captions
3-5 minutes later. Check alignment, then let the video loop and repeat.
Also test captions enabled from the start. Send diagnostics if either fails.

This is a test build. It has passed Python syntax compilation and ZIP integrity
checks, but has NOT been tested on your Windows/NTV installation.

